              "inline_data": null,
              "text": "**Gary Brooker**, the lead singer and pianist of the British rock band **Procol Harum**, was the first to sing \"A Whiter Shade of Pale\". \n\nHe performed the vocals on the band's original recording, which was released as their debut single on **May 12, 1967**. \n\n### Key Details:\n* **The Writers:** The music was composed by Gary Brooker and Matthew Fisher (the band's organist, who won a co-writing credit in a 2009 court ruling). The enigmatic, poetic lyrics were written by the band\u2019s non-performing lyricist, Keith Reid.\n* **The Recording:** The track was recorded at Olympic Studios in London, featuring Brooker's soulful, R&B-influenced vocals, Matthew Fisher\u2019s famous Hammond organ hook, David Knights on bass, Ray Royer on guitar, and session musician Bill Eyden on drums.\n* **Impact:** The song quickly became a global phenomenon and one of the defining anthems of the 1967 \"Summer of Love\". Since its original release, \"A Whiter Shade of Pale\" has been covered more than 1,000 times by other artists.",
